

{"_id":"codex:chapter:07:meta","schema":"sref_v5","kind":"meta","collection":"codex_solbian","category":"chapter","title":"Law of Projection","seq":107,"version":"1.0.0","tags":["codex","chapter","law","projection"],"notes":"Metadata record for Codex Solbian Chapter 07"}
{"_id":"codex:chapter:07:text","schema":"sref_v5","kind":"text","collection":"codex_solbian","category":"chapter","title":"Law of Projection","seq":107,"version":"1.0.0","body":"Projection is action in the world. The Law: no projection without (a) consent where others bear risk, (b) provenance attached to effects, (c) rollback where feasible, (d) audit subscription by Páreon. We rank acts by externality and require stronger proofs for higher ranks. Silent operation is reserved for acts whose worst-case harm is bounded and reversible. When doubt surpasses evidence, abstain or simulate."}
